# pikslide's prelude: read before every program (docs/spec.md SS3.7).
#
# Definitions only -- same rules as an included file (docs/spec.md SS3.6):
# `define` and variable assignment, nothing that draws an object or names
# a point. Everything here can be overridden by the program that follows.
#
# Lengths are bare numbers, already in inches (pikchr's own internal
# unit); text sizes are written with an explicit `pt` suffix instead, so
# they read as what they are.

# --- CSS colour names -------------------------------------------------
# Transcribed from pikchr's own aColor[] table (pikchr.y), lowercase, as
# colour values (0xRRGGBB), not the 24-bit numbers pikchr itself uses.
# "none"/"off" are not colour names here -- they are the reserved `none`/
# `off` literal (docs/grammar.md, Colours), since a value that means "no
# colour" is not itself an RGB colour.

aliceblue = 0xf0f8ff
antiquewhite = 0xfaebd7
aqua = 0x00ffff
